Hi Brian, Matt, Patrick and Timothy.  Thanks for taking on my project.  I'm=
 pretty flexible on being able to meet via ZOOM.  If meetings are scheduled=
 for 4:30 pm Chicago time, I'm pretty confident that any date you suggest i=
s good for me.

I urge one of you (or all) to join my group at http://tutormentorconnection=
.ning.com. That's where I've been posting ideas about mapping networks for =
more than 10 years.  On the home page you can see what I've posted about th=
e IVMOOC project.

You also should dig into the many links I  post on this page of my website.=
 https://tutormentorexchange.net/sna

As to hosting a stable website for academic and research purposes it would =
be great if you could come up with a solution that does not have me hosting=
 the site and/or that has some university ownership.  I think I could host =
the site with the same hosting service as I use for www.tutormentorexchange=
.net<http://www.tutormentorexchange.net> but I'm looking for something that=
 can exist beyond my own timeline.  I'm 79 now, so that is a concern.

Furthermore, the fact that the Fall 2025 IVMOOC team built on the 2015 team=
's work and you're building on their work, offers a roadmap for an on-going=
 project that not only collects information, but shares it, and uses it to =
bring groups together to solve problems that they can't solve by themselves=
, or in a short timeframe.

On this page you'll find four PDF visual essays showing my vision of univer=
sity involvement.  Maybe your team can bring that a bit closer to a reality=
.

Feel free to reach out by email with questions, or to schedule a ZOOM meeti=
ng.

Thank you, and good luck!

Daniel F. Bassill
